The failure of \cref{sec:cache-concurrency} starts with a truncated
file, so the tests start there too: the first half of a real pickle, as
a reader sees it while a writer is still at work.
Such a file must survive the exit hook whether or not the process
changed its cache, and once the file reads again (the writer finished),
the save must merge with it rather than give up.
The exit hook is called directly, with a registry of the test's own
([[CACHE_REGISTRY]] is replaced, so the caches of the modules imported
for the test run stay out of it).

