Unsetting the variables is not enough for [[pyalex]].
Its configuration is global state, and the OpenAlex providers write the
contact email and the key into it when they are built
(\cref{sec:openalex}).
They are built when [[scholar.providers]] is imported, and pytest
imports it while collecting, before any fixture has run, so
[[pyalex.config]] held the developer's [[SCHOLAR_EMAIL]] and
[[OPENALEX_API_KEY]] for the whole run (issue~\#160).
Every [[pyalex]] request in a test then carried the address in its
[[From]] header and the key as a bearer token, and the health probe put
the address in its [[mailto]] parameter, where it showed in failure
messages.
So the fixture empties both fields for each test and restores them
afterwards.
The key stays for the live tests, as the variables do; the email is
cleared for them too, like [[SCHOLAR_EMAIL]].
[[pyalex]] is imported inside the fixture, never at module level, since
the conftest must not load anything before it has redirected the
directories (\cref{sec:conftest-import-time}).

