\subsection{Isolating import time and exit time}
\label{sec:conftest-import-time}

A fixture only covers the time while a test runs, and the caches are
also read before the first test and written after the last one.
Each provider module loads its cache when it is imported
([[load_cache]], \cref{sec:cache-autosave}), and pytest imports the test
modules, and with them every provider, while collecting, before any
fixture has set [[SCHOLAR_CACHE_DIR]].
The tests then fill and empty those in-memory caches, and the exit hook
writes every registered cache to [[get_cache_dir()]] once the
interpreter exits.
By then monkeypatch has restored the environment, so before this was
fixed every test run replaced the developer's real cache with whatever
the tests had left in memory: the cached search results, which make
re-running a session's searches free, and the language-model output that
[[cache clear]] deliberately keeps (\cref{sec:cache-keep-llm}) were
lost, and test entries such as [[10.1234/test]] took their place
(\url{https://github.com/dbosk/scholar/issues/132}).

The fix gives the whole test process directories of its own before
anything can read the real ones.
The conftest is imported before any test module, so setting the
variables there, first thing, is early enough for the import-time loads.
That holds only while nothing in the conftest imports [[scholar]] at
module level, which is why the chunk opens the file and checks that
[[scholar.cache]] is not loaded yet, instead of trusting a convention.
When the exit hook runs, monkeypatch has restored [[SCHOLAR_CACHE_DIR]]
to the process directory rather than unsetting it.
The data directory gets the same treatment, since nothing guarantees
that every module reads it only inside a test.
The per-test directories of [[isolate_cache]] stay: they keep the tests
from seeing each other's files.
Python runs exit handlers in reverse order of registration, and the
conftest registers its clean-up before [[scholar.cache]] registers the
save, so the caches are written into the process directory first and
then removed together with it.

