Rate-limit pacing must not slow the test suite down: once providers
declare request rates (\cref{ch:ratelimit}), every mocked multi-page
search would otherwise spend real wall-clock time sleeping between
requests.
We therefore disable the limiter's sleep seam globally.
The pacing \emph{behaviour} is still verified---the rate-limit module's
own tests replace the same seam with a recorder and assert on the
requested sleep durations.

<<[[conftest.py]]>>=

@pytest.fixture(autouse=True)
def no_rate_limit_sleep(monkeypatch):
    """Disable real rate-limit pacing sleeps during tests."""
    monkeypatch.setattr(
        "scholar.ratelimit._sleep", lambda seconds: None
    )
