\subsection{Gating live API tests}
\label{sec:live-tests}

Each provider ships an [[@pytest.mark.integration]] test that hits the real
API.  These are invaluable for catching breakage that mocks cannot---an expired
API key, a provider changing its response shape---but they are slow, flaky, and
sometimes require credentials, so they must stay \emph{off} during an ordinary
[[pytest]] run.

Rather than hard-[[@pytest.mark.skip]] each one (which makes them impossible to
run at all without editing source), we gate them behind a [[--run-live]] flag.
When the flag is absent we attach a skip marker to every [[integration]]-marked
item during collection; passing [[--run-live]] lets them through.  This keeps
the default run fully mocked and offline while making the live suite a single
flag away: [[pytest --run-live -m integration]].

<<[[conftest.py]]>>=
def pytest_addoption(parser):
    """Register the ``--run-live`` flag that enables integration tests."""
    parser.addoption(
        "--run-live",
        action="store_true",
        default=False,
        help="run integration tests that make real API calls",
    )


def pytest_collection_modifyitems(config, items):
    """Skip integration tests unless ``--run-live`` was passed."""
    if config.getoption("--run-live"):
        return
    skip_live = pytest.mark.skip(
        reason="needs --run-live (makes real API calls)"
    )
    for item in items:
        if "integration" in item.keywords:
            item.add_marker(skip_live)
@
